{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1516","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Baby Ehab Plays with Permutations"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This time around, Baby Ehab will play with permutations. He has $$$n$$$ cubes arranged in a row, with numbers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ written on them. He'll make "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$j$$$ operations. In each operation, he'll pick up $$$2$$$ cubes and switch their positions."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"He's wondering: how many different sequences of cubes can I have at the end? Since Baby Ehab is a turbulent person, he doesn't know how many operations he'll make, so he wants the answer for every possible $$$j$$$ between $$$1$$$ and $$$k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains $$$2$$$ integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 10^9$$$, $$$1 \\le k \\le 200$$$) — the number of cubes Baby Ehab has, and the parameter $$$k$$$ from the statement."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$k$$$ space-separated integers. The $$$i$$$-th of them is the number of possible sequences you can end up with if you do exactly $$$i$$$ operations. Since this number can be very large, print the remainder when it's divided by $$$10^9+7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 1 1 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 3 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 12 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, there are $$$3$$$ sequences he can get after $$$1$$$ swap, because there are $$$3$$$ pairs of cubes he can swap. Also, there are $$$3$$$ sequences he can get after $$$2$$$ swaps:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1,2,3]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[3,1,2]$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[2,3,1]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1516E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1516/problem/E"}